From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: George Whewell <georgerw@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 21:05:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 0061] media: sophgo: allow double-buffered SG2002 CSI capture

vb2 adds one buffer to min_queued_buffers when sizing a REQBUFS queue.
The SG2002 driver set that minimum to two, so an application asking for
two buffers received three.  A double-buffered queue is sufficient: one
buffer is active in the VI DMA engine while the other remains queued,
and the driver's scratch buffer already absorbs frames if userspace does
not return a buffer before the following interrupt.

Allow the two-buffer queue by setting min_queued_buffers to one.  This
saves one order-11 RAW12 allocation on the 256 MiB LicheeRV camera node,
where the 32 MiB shared media pool also holds Coda980 state.  Applications
requesting three or more buffers are unchanged.

Signed-off-by: George Whewell <georgerw@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/sophgo/sg2002-capture.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/sophgo/sg2002-capture.c b/drivers/media/platform/sophgo/sg2002-capture.c
index 90f35bb1d..2f72a55d1 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/sophgo/sg2002-capture.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/sophgo/sg2002-capture.c
@@ -1352,7 +1352,7 @@ static int sg2002_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	q->ops = &sg2002_vb2_ops;
 	q->mem_ops = &vb2_dma_contig_memops;
 	q->timestamp_flags = V4L2_BUF_FLAG_TIMESTAMP_MONOTONIC;
-	q->min_queued_buffers = 2;
+	q->min_queued_buffers = 1;
 	q->dev = cap->dev;
 	ret = vb2_queue_init(q);
 	if (ret)
